write('zero-disclosure-browser-report.md',`# Browser zero-disclosure report\\n\\n**RESULT: BLOCKED — no supported browser session was available for this exact source state.**\\n\\nThe deterministic projection suite is ${sourceChecks.passed}/${sourceChecks.total} PASS. That proves the fixture authorization functions, not rendered DOM, browser storage, accessibility tree, downloads or production APIs. The ten required lab profiles were defined and are listed below.\\n\\n| PROFILE | DOM | NAVIGATION | MOBILE NAV | HUB | GLOBAL SEARCH | AI SEARCH | COMMAND | HELP | DASHBOARD/KPI | ACTION CENTER | NOTIFICATIONS | FAVORITES/BOOKMARKS/RECENTS | SAVED VIEWS | REPORTS | COLUMNS/EXPORTS | DEEP LINKS | RESULT |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n${s.testProfiles.map(p=>'| '+p+' | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | Browser unavailable; source projection only |').join('\\n')}\\n\\n## Required purge scenarios\\n\\nSession changes call \`purgePrivilegedProjectionState()\` before the new context is presented and on sign-out. The purge targets favorites, bookmarks, recents, saved views/searches, dashboard configuration, record selection and fixture projection keys. Browser storage and DOM re-projection remain BLOCKED for independent acceptance.\\n\\n## Neutral assignment-pending state\\n\\nProvisional and no-permission sessions render: “Your Daenem identity is ready. Your assigned workspace will appear after your access setup is completed.” No hidden-module count, name, catalogue or permission error is shown.\\n`);
write('accessibility-report.md',`# Accessibility review\n\n**STATUS: BLOCKED for complete acceptance; code-level safeguards are present.**\n\n| CHECK | RESULT | EVIDENCE / LIMIT |\n|---|---|---|\n| Keyboard traversal / logical tab order | BLOCKED | Requires supported browser walkthrough on all 26 priority screens. |\n| Visible focus | PASS_IN_SOURCE | Focus-visible tokens and labeled controls are present; browser contrast/focus capture pending. |\n| Dialog focus trap / Escape / drawer focus | BLOCKED | Radix dialogs/sheets are used, but no current browser evidence packet is available. |\n| Accessible names / labels / errors / status text | PASS_IN_SOURCE | Auth, fields, errors and live status text have explicit labels in source; independent screen-reader pass pending. |\n| 200% zoom / reflow | BLOCKED | Requires browser viewport and zoom evidence. |\n| Contrast and image-overlay contrast | BLOCKED | Gallery/Panorama/Nightfall/Command fixes are source-updated, but fresh loaded captures are unavailable. |\n| Reduced motion | PASS_IN_SOURCE | Reduced-motion media rule disables animations/transitions/scroll behavior. |\n| Touch targets / mobile navigation | BLOCKED | Requires supported device emulation and full matrix. |\n`);
write('performance-report.md',`# Performance review\n\n**STATUS: BLOCKED for browser metrics; build and asset bounds are verified.**\n\n- Production build: PASS (Vinext build completed for client, server, RSC and SSR environments).\n- Runtime image candidates: 640 / 1280 / 2560 / 3840 WebP; raw native originals are not in srcset.\n- Native originals remain provenance assets; the browser is not directed to a >13K original for ordinary 4K displays.\n- LCP, CLS, INP, route-transition timing, 4K/mobile transfer capture and large-table virtualization timing: BLOCKED because no supported browser session was available for this source state.\n- No performance number is invented.\n`);
write('fixture-coherence-report.md',`# Fixture coherence report\n\n**STATUS: PARTIAL LAB / PRODUCTION MAPPING REQUIRED**\n\nCentral seedRecords() plus enterpriseFixtures provides typed module envelopes and shared records. The closure pass adds source-derived PO commitment, bakery quantity/cash variance, authorized projections and a local atomic goods-receipt operation that updates receipt, linked PO received quantity, inventory and history together when identifiers match.\n\nLinked scenarios represented: expense → approval → procurement → PO → receipt → inventory; bakery custody → remittance → investigation; candidate → vacancy → provisional identity → onboarding; printing job → material/QC/profit; trip → POD/profit; property collection → ROI; attendance → employee home; profile gaps → Action Center.\n\nThis is not a production transaction system. Durable D1/R2/Worker adapters, idempotency, concurrency, immutable audit and reconciliation remain integration gaps.\n`);
write('component-inventory.md',`# Component inventory\n\nThe Site keeps the V3 React/Vinext foundation and adds: AuthV3 + V3 Sign-In Studio; ten sign-in compositions; neutral assignment-pending surface; profile and attendance workspaces; specialized procurement, PO, goods receipt, stock transfer, borrowing, bakery accountability, technology services and vacancy desks; Staff Messaging; productivity governance; work-location policy; salary adjustments; controlled import; dashboard personalization; versioned builders; authorized enterprise tables; saved views/files/audit; and source-derived fixture mutation.\n\nShared primitives remain Panel, Btn, Pick, RecordsTable, Steps, Timeline, Metric, Bars, Viz, RouteMap, Tabs, Dialog and state boundaries. Permission projection occurs before navigation, search, record fields, exports and AI context.\n`);
write('design-system.md',`# Design system\n\nThe V3 visual language uses high-contrast navy/blue enterprise surfaces, restrained white panels, green/amber/red status badges, generous 12–16px radii and responsive grid primitives. Sign-in compositions preserve the supplied bright/architectural direction while keeping an opaque, visually dominant auth card.\n\nTheme, layout, density, motion and widget composition are independent. Themes include Light/Daylight, Dark/Midnight and Auto-compatible preference behavior; motion supports Off, Calm, Balanced and Expressive; layouts are the ten named structural profiles; presets combine starting values without changing permission.\n\nAll source photography is credited in image-assets.json; Nigeria/West Africa appears in Lagos Marina, Abuja Towers, Ibadan Senate and Lagos bridge contexts. The images are not presented as Daenem facilities.\n`);
write('auth-flow-map.md',`# Authentication and identity flow\n\nUsername/email + password remains the default sign-in. OTP is limited to signup verification, recovery and future approved high-risk step-up demonstration. Microsoft and Google are optional future federation and display “Configured provider required” until integrated.\n\nSignup collects legal/full name, phone, work email, requested company, department/work area, job/position/work details, unique username, optional existing-employee reference, password/confirmation and policy acceptance. Verification uses a six-digit local demo code. Duplicate username/employee matches are blocked. Verification creates a provisional identity; operational access remains absent until an administrator assigns company, role, module, field and record scope.\n\nStep-up is demonstrated for sensitive bank detail or Access Control changes and is explicitly labelled a demonstration; no production MFA provider is connected.\n`);
write('offline-contract.md',`# Offline contract\n\nThe Site represents Offline, Stale, Sync Conflict and Integration Unavailable states with local fixture controls. Local mutations carry a revision, audit history and “Waiting to Sync” label where applicable. Production offline sync, background location, push delivery, replay idempotency and conflict persistence are not claimed; map them to existing Worker/D1/R2 contracts before implementation.\n`);
