write('known-gaps.md',`# Known gaps and acceptance status\n\n## Final status\n\n**STAFFPORTAL_SITES_ACCEPTANCE_CLOSURE_INCOMPLETE**\n\nThe source foundation builds and the deterministic suite passes, but Site-owned acceptance is not complete because the supported browser preview was unavailable for this exact source state. No Critical/High Site-owned gap is silently treated as closed.\n\n## A. Site-owned acceptance gaps\n\n1. **Browser zero-disclosure evidence — Critical — BLOCKED.** Source projection and purge code pass; rendered DOM, mobile navigation, command palette, search, help, AI, exports, deep links and browser storage need live profile capture.\n2. **Priority visual matrix — High — BLOCKED.** All 182 required rows are present with BLOCKED results; no stale pre-fix screenshot is reused.\n3. **Accessibility walkthrough — High — BLOCKED.** Keyboard, focus trapping, zoom, touch and screen-reader evidence require supported browser capture.\n4. **Performance acceptance — High — BLOCKED.** LCP/CLS/INP, route transition, transfer and virtualization measurements were not available.\n5. **Domain depth — High — PARTIAL.** Purpose-built Site surfaces are present, but end-to-end production-like linked workflows, immutable ledger behavior and all mature HR/ERP pages still need acceptance.\n6. **Builder acceptance — High — PARTIAL.** Local consumers are wired, but browser verification that each published definition affects the target experience remains pending.\n7. **Fixture coherence — High — PARTIAL.** Core linked scenarios and atomic goods-receipt simulation are present; full domain conservation and dependent summary coverage need broader acceptance.\n\n## B. Production-integration gaps (allowed, specified)\n\n- Existing Worker/RBAC identity mapping, tenant/record/field authorization and server-side zero disclosure.\n- D1 typed schema, migrations, transactions, revisions, idempotency and reconciliation for finance, payroll, procurement, inventory, bakery, printing, logistics and properties.\n- R2 file classes, scanning, versioning, retention, legal hold and scoped byte delivery.\n- Email, notification, federation, GPS/camera, weather, maps and accounting/payroll provider contracts.\n- Immutable audit and production monitoring.\n- PWA/background sync and any device capabilities.\n\nThese are not attempted inside Sites. See production-gap-map.csv and integration-contracts.csv.\n`);
write('START-HERE.md',`# Daenem Staff Portal V3.1 Sites acceptance-closure packet\n\n**STAFFPORTAL_SITES_ACCEPTANCE_CLOSURE_INCOMPLETE**\n\nThis packet continues the existing V3 source. It does not restart the Site, remove valid work, write GitHub, write production Cloudflare/D1/R2 or deploy.\n\nRead in order:\n\n1. MASTER-COMPLETION-REPORT.md\n2. CHECKPOINT-PROVENANCE.json\n3. zero-disclosure-browser-report.md\n4. responsive-evidence.csv and accessibility/performance reports\n5. requirement-traceability.csv\n6. domain/entity/API/workflow/rule catalogs\n7. known-gaps.md and production-gap-map.csv\n\nSource checks: ${sourceChecks.passed}/${sourceChecks.total} deterministic PASS; source contract checks: 28/28 PASS. Browser-level and visual acceptance are explicitly BLOCKED where unsupported. All records and images are fictional/demo or credited public sources; do not enter real credentials.\n`);
