write('MASTER-COMPLETION-REPORT.md',`# Master completion report\n\n**STAFFPORTAL_SITES_ACCEPTANCE_CLOSURE_INCOMPLETE**\n\nThe existing V3 foundation was continued. This closure pass corrects the Nigerian/global sign-in balance, replaces the competing sign-in composer with V3 Sign-In Studio, adds responsive image derivatives and focal-point delivery, completes signup/claim fields and policy acceptance, adds neutral provisional/no-permission behavior and stale projection purge, introduces named post-auth presets, purpose-built procurement/custody/bakery/technology/vacancy workspaces, local builder consumers, Staff Messaging, governed productivity, work-location policy, salary adjustments, controlled import and dashboard personalization, and records atomic local receipt/stock mutation contracts.\n\n## Evidence summary\n\n- ${model.modules.length} concrete workspace/module definitions (the six new closure modules are included; route count was not inflated).\n- ${sourceChecks.passed}/${sourceChecks.total} deterministic source checks PASS; 28/28 source-contract checks PASS.\n- 3,160 source requirement clauses preserved in requirement-traceability.csv.\n- ${entities.length} entity catalog rows, ${opRows.length} semantic operation rows, ${ruleRows.length} business rules, ${validationRows.length} validation rules, ${auditRows.length} audit events, ${notificationRows.length} notification events and ${metricRows.length} report metrics generated from current Site concepts.\n- Ten sign-in records use native 4K+ originals; four are Nigerian/West African contexts (Lagos Marina, Abuja Towers, Ibadan Senate and Lagos bridge). Runtime candidates are WebP 640/1280/2560/3840 only; raw originals remain source provenance.\n- All 182 priority responsive rows are present and explicitly BLOCKED because no supported browser preview was available for this exact source state.\n- Browser zero-disclosure, accessibility interaction, performance timing and fresh final visual captures are BLOCKED, not claimed.\n\n## Site-owned vs production integration\n\nSite-owned acceptance remains incomplete where live browser/evidence or deeper workflow acceptance is missing. Production gaps are specified in the catalogs and are not attempted.\n\nGITHUB MODIFIED: NO\n\nPRODUCTION CLOUDFLARE MODIFIED: NO\n\nPRODUCTION D1 WRITTEN: NO\n\nPRODUCTION R2 WRITTEN: NO\n\nPRODUCTION DEPLOYED: NO\n\nREADY FOR PRODUCTION: NO\n\nREADY FOR INDEPENDENT ACCEPTANCE: NO — browser/visual gates remain BLOCKED.\n`);
write('handoff-notes.md',`# Handoff notes\n\nContinue from the exact SOURCE_COMMIT in CHECKPOINT-PROVENANCE.json. The Site source is the existing internal Sites repository; no GitHub write or production deployment was performed. The saved Site version, if present, is a source checkpoint only.\n\nIndependent review should first bind a supported private browser preview to this source commit, run the ten zero-disclosure profiles and 26×7 responsive matrix, refresh Gallery/Panorama/Nightfall/Command captures after images/fonts/data settle, then validate the domain scenarios and catalogs against the existing Staff Portal Worker/RBAC contracts.\n`);
write('database-mapping-notes.md',`# Database mapping notes\n\nThe entity and operation catalogs are typed conceptual contracts derived from the Site. RecordData is a fixture envelope, not a production schema. Map each entity to existing D1 tables or approved new schema only after read-only backend inspection. Preserve tenant/company, record, field, specialized capability, revision, idempotency and audit constraints.\n`);
